fencedThat reproduction is the actual bug: documents whose bare header starts with `depends:` are not considered front matter at all. The current bare-frontmatter detector only accepts a first line of `title: `, so `depends:\n  - foo` is parsed as body text; fenced YAML bypasses that detector and works.

I’m changing the detector to recognize a leading bare YAML mapping block, with conservative key-line validation plus YAML parse confirmation, then updating the outdated “no title first line” test expectation.
